{"id": "section-body-27102", "title": "Depression", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-three", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MENTAL HEALTH CONDITIONS", "Psychiatric Disorders in Pregnancy", "Depression"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-27102", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Depression", "runs": [{"text": "Depression"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "341"}}, {"id": "body-27103", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Several risk factors and psychosocial correlates have been identified as contributing to depression during pregnancy, like; Previous history of depression, discontinuation of medication(s) by a woman who has a history of depression, a previous history of postpartum depression, and a family history of depression.", "runs": [{"text": "Several risk factors and psychosocial correlates have been identified as contributing to depression during pregnancy, like; Previous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "depression,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "discontinuation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medication(s)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "woman"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "who"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "has"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "depression,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "previous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history of postpartum depression, and a family history of depression."}]}, {"id": "body-27105", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Several key psychosocial correlates may also contribute to depression during pregnancy: a negative attitude toward the pregnancy, a lack of social support, maternal stress associated with negative life events, and a partner or family member who is unhappy about the pregnancy. The relationship between maternal depression and early childhood problems may be part of a sequence that starts with depressive symptoms during pregnancy.", "runs": [{"text": "Several key psychosocial correlates may also contribute to depression during pregnancy: a negative attitude toward the pregnancy,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a lack of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "social"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "support,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maternal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stress associated with negative life events,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and a partner"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "family member"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "who is unhappy about the pregnancy. The relationship between maternal depression and early childhood problems may be part of a sequence that starts with depressive symptoms during pregnancy."}]}, {"id": "body-27107", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-27108", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Psychotherapies", "runs": [{"text": "Psychotherapies"}]}, {"id": "body-27109", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Cognitive behavioral therapy", "runs": [{"text": "Cognitive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "behavioral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapy"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "341"}}, {"id": "body-27110", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Interpersonal psychotherapy", "runs": [{"text": "Interpersonal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "psychotherapy"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "341"}}, {"id": "body-27111", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Education and support are also important, particularly as pregnancy is a unique experience for women, some of whom may not know what to expect.", "runs": [{"text": "Education"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"